and `BuiltDiagramSet` owns explicitly constructed numerators and grouping.
The staged internal generator uses the current admitted numerator/template cache,
not the obsolete compiled-interaction implementation. Raw index validation and
tensor admission precede conservation reduction; checked expression rewrites
retain interfaces and hidden zero/index history. Dynamic rules enter once in
their actual owner frame. Static template admission remains outside cache write
guards, concurrent publication keeps one shared template, and localization uses
the current injective transport and declared/inferred port ordering.

The current spectator/scoped-partner protections, colour-only completion and
scalar eligibility proof remain on their existing owners. The transplant does
not restore the superseded zero-colour proof helper or a second admission path.

The native MathML/static/optional-widget display remains authoritative. The
shared Kurvst mark engine arrives as a source17 prerequisite; this is not the
later source38 replacement. The live drawing view keeps its existing Python
identity; the newly introduced typed generation callback is
`GenerationDiagramView` to avoid registering two owners under `DiagramView`.
Python consumers use the current declarative graph-node factory and staged
request/build calls. No compatibility implementation is retained.

